  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and lightheadedness consistent with supraventricular tachycardia, occurring against a background of known atherosclerotic heart disease of the native coronary artery (I25.10). Mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is ordered to capture intermittent arrhythmic events and correlate symptoms with rhythm disturbances in an outpatient setting. This service is medically necessary to evaluate the recurrent palpitations and lightheadedness in a patient with a documented history of supraventricular tachycardia and coronary artery disease."
